# Engine-level cancel with a native call running (internal/unreal/session:
# actor.go cancelTurn/checkCancel/submit, gate.go Park/CancelInflight/
# Respond; render.tsx groupTurns and app.tsx NativeCall for where a row
# lands and what it says). One engine session, the Runtime seen from its
# history: Esc / ctrl+c in the TUI, or Runtime.Cancel.
#
# A cancel (§9.7) lands the steers already typed, parks the turn's calls
# and every input id sent (Gate.Park: a request that answers only parked
# things is muted, answered empty without the provider), cuts the request
# in flight (CancelInflight: the partial text is the answer), cancels the
# turn's running calls' ops, and waits for them to report, at most
# cancelWait (1 s). Then "cancelled" and "done" are written together.
#
# Where the code disagrees with the mapped model, the code wins:
#   - "cancelling_deadline_passed" is not a state: the timer posts to the
#     actor and evaluate closes the cancel in the same event
#     (CancelWaitExpires). "cancelled_done" is idle with closes == 1.
#   - PartialAnswer is not an action: the Gate answers the cut request at
#     once with what streamed, so Stop takes req to False in one step.
#   - Page.CatchUp is not an action: groupTurns is a pure function of the
#     rows, so a catch-up places a row where the live view did; `row` is
#     that placement.
#   - A late row does not land in the cancelled turn (the mapped
#     invariant): after the cancel's done, groupTurns puts it in a turn of
#     its own with no prompt ("orphan"), in the wake turn it starts
#     ("wake"), or in the next turn's body ("next").
#   - An adopted call reporting during the cancel is job news: it is never
#     parked, so its request goes to the provider and unparks everything
#     the cancel parked (Gate.Respond clears pCalls). JobFinishes is
#     allowed only while cancelling; a job reporting at other times is the
#     background flows'.
#   - In serve, Stop is a SIGINT and the child exits after the cancel's
#     done (stop_interrupt.fizz), and the page refuses a prompt while
#     stopping: late rows and PromptDuringCancel are reachable in the TUI
#     and in-process, not through the web.
#   - A call's result never cuts a request in flight (only an input
#     does): it waits for that request's answer and goes out with the
#     next one (`waiting`). A prompt or a steer sent meanwhile carries it;
#     a cancel parks it with the rest of m.Reasons, so it is muted.
#   - A cancel closes on the report of the last call it waited for,
#     before that call's result asks the model: the result opens a wake
#     turn of its own (or goes out with the prompt the close opened).
#   - A pending cancel's turn cuts the request in flight, as any cancel
#     does, and parks what is pending.
#   (Found by the MBT walks against the engine,
#   tests/model/mbt/engine_cancel_mid_call_test.go; the spec first had
#   the result asking at once and the cancel waiting on its request.)
#
# Fields (Engine role):
#   turn      idle | open | cancelling (a.open / a.cancelling)
#   wake      the open turn was opened by the engine (openWake), not a prompt
#   turns     user prompts so far, bounded by MAX_TURNS
#   closes    close records (done, or cancelled+done) of the current turn
#   req       a request is in flight (m.Inflight)
#   call      the one native call: none | running | cancelling (its turn's
#             cancel is waiting on it) | late (the cancel closed without it)
#   parked    that call's result is covered by the Gate's park
#   waiting   that call reported while a request was in flight; its result
#             goes out once that request has answered
#   row       where the cancelled call's end row landed: "" | turn (before
#             cancelled/done) | orphan | wake | next. A row that lands
#             between turns while a request is in flight is "orphan"
#             until the wake turn its result opens takes it in.
#   shows     what that row says: "" | cancelled (canceled: true) | ok
#   steer     one steer: none | typed (Runtime.Steer, not yet landed) |
#             queued (steerQ, waiting on the request boundary) | note
#             (a.notes: prefixed to the next prompt) | parked (sent, its
#             request muted; in context) | delivered (the model has it)
#   pending   a prompt submitted while cancelling (a.pending)
#   pending_cancel  a cancel that arrived before its turn opened (cancelAt)
#   quiet     a cancel happened and no prompt has reached the model since
#   job       an adopted call from an earlier turn: running | reported
#   leak      a request answering the cancelled call reached the provider
#             while quiet and no turn was open
#   stray     a model reply was recorded while no turn was open

---
deadlock_detection: false
---

MAX_TURNS = 2

role Engine:
    action Init:
        self.turn = "idle"
        self.wake = False
        self.turns = 0
        self.closes = 0
        self.req = False
        self.call = "none"
        self.row = ""
        self.shows = ""
        self.steer = "none"
        self.parked = False
        self.pending = False
        self.pending_cancel = False
        self.job = "running"
        self.stray = False
        self.leak = False
        self.quiet = False
        self.waiting = False

    atomic func open_user_turn():
        self.turns = self.turns + 1
        self.turn = "open"
        self.wake = False
        self.closes = 0
        if self.steer == "note" or self.steer == "parked":
            self.steer = "delivered"
        # Either way a waiting result is taken: parked by the cancel below,
        # or carried by the prompt's request.
        self.waiting = False
        if self.pending_cancel:
            # cancelTurn right after startTurn: the request in flight is
            # cut and the new input parked with what is pending.
            self.pending_cancel = False
            self.quiet = True
            self.turn = "idle"
            self.closes = 1
            self.req = False
        else:
            self.parked = False
            self.quiet = False
            self.req = True

    atomic func close_cancel():
        self.turn = "idle"
        self.closes = self.closes + 1
        if self.pending:
            self.pending = False
            self.open_user_turn()

    atomic func asked():
        if self.steer == "parked":
            self.steer = "delivered"
        self.parked = False
        if self.turn == "idle":
            self.turn = "open"
            self.wake = True
            self.closes = 0
        self.req = True

    # The waiting result goes out once the request it waited on answered,
    # unless that answer already led to a request that carries it.
    atomic func send_waiting():
        if self.waiting:
            self.waiting = False
            if not self.req:
                if self.quiet and self.turn != "open":
                    self.leak = True
                if self.turn == "idle" and self.row == "orphan":
                    self.row = "wake"
                self.asked()

    atomic func reported(shows):
        if self.call == "cancelling":
            self.row = "turn"
        elif self.turn == "idle" and (self.parked or self.req):
            self.row = "orphan"
        elif self.turn == "idle":
            self.row = "wake"
        else:
            self.row = "next"
        own = self.call == "cancelling"
        self.call = "none"
        self.shows = shows
        if self.parked:
            self.parked = False
            if own and self.turn == "cancelling" and not self.req:
                self.close_cancel()
        elif own and self.turn == "cancelling" and not self.req:
            # The close comes first; a prompt it opens carries the result
            # (or, a pending cancel's, parks it).
            opens = self.pending
            self.close_cancel()
            if not opens:
                if self.quiet:
                    self.leak = True
                self.asked()
        elif self.req:
            self.waiting = True
        else:
            if self.quiet and self.turn != "open":
                self.leak = True
            self.asked()

    atomic action Prompt:
        require self.turn == "idle" and self.turns < MAX_TURNS
        self.open_user_turn()

    atomic action StopBeforeSubmitCrosses:
        require self.turn == "idle" and not self.pending_cancel and self.turns < MAX_TURNS
        self.pending_cancel = True

    atomic fair action PendingCancelLapses:
        require self.pending_cancel
        self.pending_cancel = False

    atomic action Steer:
        require self.turn == "open" and self.steer == "none"
        self.steer = "typed"

    atomic fair action SteerLands:
        require self.turn == "open" and self.steer == "typed"
        if self.req:
            self.steer = "queued"
        else:
            self.steer = "delivered"
            self.req = True

    atomic action CallStarts:
        require self.turn == "open" and self.req and self.call == "none"
        self.call = "running"
        self.req = False
        if self.steer == "queued":
            self.steer = "delivered"
            self.req = True
        self.send_waiting()

    atomic action CallReturns:
        require self.turn == "open" and self.call == "running" and not self.req
        self.call = "none"
        self.req = True

    atomic fair action ModelAnswers:
        require self.req
        self.req = False
        if self.turn == "idle":
            self.stray = True
        elif self.turn == "cancelling":
            if self.call != "cancelling":
                self.close_cancel()
        elif self.steer == "queued":
            self.steer = "delivered"
            self.req = True
        elif self.call != "running" and not self.waiting:
            self.turn = "idle"
            self.closes = self.closes + 1
        self.send_waiting()

    atomic action Stop:
        require self.turn == "open" or self.turn == "cancelling"
        if self.turn == "open":
            if self.steer == "typed":
                if self.req:
                    self.steer = "note"
                else:
                    self.steer = "parked"
            elif self.steer == "queued":
                self.steer = "note"
            self.quiet = True
            self.req = False
            # a result waiting on the cut request is in m.Reasons: parked
            self.waiting = False
            if self.call == "running":
                self.parked = True
                self.call = "cancelling"
                self.turn = "cancelling"
            else:
                self.close_cancel()

    atomic action PromptDuringCancel:
        require self.turn == "cancelling" and not self.pending and self.turns < MAX_TURNS
        self.pending = True

    atomic action CallReportsCanceled:
        require self.call == "cancelling" or self.call == "late"
        self.reported("cancelled")

    atomic action CallIgnoresCancel:
        require self.call == "cancelling" or self.call == "late"
        self.reported("ok")

    atomic fair action CancelWaitExpires:
        require self.turn == "cancelling"
        if self.call == "cancelling":
            self.call = "late"
        self.close_cancel()

    atomic action JobFinishes:
        require self.job == "running" and self.turn == "cancelling"
        self.job = "reported"
        self.asked()

action Init:
    engine = Engine()

# cancelled and done are written once per turn, together (checkCancel);
# a second Stop while cancelling is a no-op (cancelTurn returns).
always assertion CancelClosesOnce:
    return engine.closes <= 1

# A call that reports canceled shows Cancelled, never a failure
# (NativeCall: failed = !canceled && ...).
always assertion CancelledRowNeverFails:
    return engine.shows != "failed"

# A steer typed before Stop is recorded and reaches the model with the
# next prompt: as a note in its payload, or in context as a parked input.
always assertion SteerReachesNextInput:
    return not (engine.turn == "open" and not engine.wake and engine.steer in ("note", "parked"))

# A turn cancel leaves adopted calls running (cs.calls skips them).
always assertion AdoptedJobSurvivesCancel:
    return engine.job != "cancelled"

# A prompt sent while cancelling waits in a.pending and opens its own
# turn in the same evaluate that writes the cancel's done.
always assertion PendingOnlyWhileCancelling:
    return not engine.pending or engine.turn == "cancelling"

# A cancel closes within cancelWait: its timer is fair.
always eventually assertion CancelCloses:
    return engine.turn != "cancelling"

always eventually assertion PendingOpens:
    return not engine.pending

# Mapped claims the code does not keep. They are left out so the check
# stays green; each is a finding, with fizz's counterexample:
#
# "After a cancel no request reaches the provider until a new input"
# (not engine.leak) fails twice over:
#   1. Prompt, CallStarts, Stop, JobFinishes, CallReportsCanceled,
#      ModelAnswers: the adopted job's request unparks, so the cancelled
#      call's result, which waited on that request, goes to the provider
#      once it answers, in a wake turn the cancel's close did not stop.
#   2. Prompt, CallStarts, Stop, PromptDuringCancel, CancelWaitExpires,
#      Stop, CallReportsCanceled: the second cancel parks only its own
#      turn's calls, not the late call the first cancel let go of, so its
#      result opens a wake turn after the second Esc.
#
# "A late call row is attributed to the cancelled turn" (row is "" or
# turn) fails: Prompt, CallStarts, Stop, CancelWaitExpires,
# CallReportsCanceled puts the row after done, in a prompt-less turn.
#
# "No model reply after done" (not engine.stray) fails: Prompt,
# CallStarts, Stop, JobFinishes, CancelWaitExpires, ModelAnswers: the
# deadline closed the cancel with the job's request in flight, and its
# reply (and any calls it makes) is recorded with no turn open.
